  "worked_solution": "Since $x$ and $y$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8x,y\u27e9 & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot (2\\cdot (-2))+k\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-3-16+k \\\\  & =k-19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $\u27e8x,y\u27e9=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8x,y\u27e9 & =0 \\\\ k-19 & =0 \\\\ k & =19\\end{aligned}\n$$",
